1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,942
Welcome to PulseTwin, a personal blood pressure digital twin built for the Digital Twin Challenge.

2
00:00:06,942 --> 00:00:14,346
The central idea is simple: daily observations should help us ask better questions about possible futures.

3
00:00:14,346 --> 00:00:22,676
This prototype combines a working dashboard, an interpretable personal model, a daily state update, and an evidence report.

4
00:00:22,676 --> 00:00:35,634
In this walkthrough, we will follow a synthetic profile from observations to a scenario, inspect the model behind the curve, and test the workflow with an imported file.

5
00:00:35,634 --> 00:00:37,948
Every example uses generated data.

6
00:00:37,948 --> 00:00:42,576
No patient outcomes, clinical accuracy, or treatment benefits are claimed.

7
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:48,592
The voiceover is synthesized, and the interface captures come from the running application.

8
00:00:48,592 --> 00:00:56,922
The source code, model card, architecture, tests, and presentation accompany the prototype so reviewers can reproduce the demonstration.

9
00:00:59,422 --> 00:01:07,658
Imagine a person with three months of blood pressure readings, step counts, sleep notes, dietary estimates, and self-reported stress.

10
00:01:07,658 --> 00:01:15,894
A conventional chart can show a trend, but it cannot explain how these measurements fit together for that individual.

11
00:01:15,894 --> 00:01:21,096
A generic wellness score often hides the relationship behind a single number.

12
00:01:21,096 --> 00:01:31,933
PulseTwin explores a different interaction: make the personal model visible, let the user specify a hypothetical scenario, and show the uncertainty next to the result.

13
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:37,568
This is a research problem rather than a promise to lower blood pressure.

14
00:01:37,568 --> 00:01:43,636
Many important drivers are unmeasured, and lifestyle variables can be correlated with each other.

15
00:01:43,636 --> 00:01:47,971
Our design treats those limitations as part of the product.

16
00:01:47,971 --> 00:01:54,040
The goal is to support informed questions, not to turn observational patterns into prescriptions.

17
00:01:56,540 --> 00:02:05,625
The selected use case is longitudinal cardiometabolic research and education, with systolic blood pressure as the single modeled outcome.

18
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:15,666
A researcher or an authorized user can inspect how a person's observations relate to daily habits and explore a conditional future.

19
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:22,839
We deliberately avoid a broad health score, disease diagnosis, medication recommendations, and automated clinical decisions.

20
00:02:22,839 --> 00:02:30,012
A narrow outcome makes the model easier to inspect and the prototype easier to validate.

21
00:02:30,012 --> 00:02:38,141
The application does not contain a physician workflow, electronic health record integration, or a live wearable connection.

22
00:02:38,141 --> 00:02:42,922
Those are possible future integrations, not features we claim today.

23
00:02:42,922 --> 00:02:51,051
The complete implemented loop is observation ingestion, validation, personal fitting, residual state updating, scenario simulation, and review.

24
00:02:51,051 --> 00:02:56,311
Keeping this scope explicit is essential to evaluating the submission fairly.

25
00:02:58,811 --> 00:03:00,961
Here is the running dashboard.

26
00:03:00,961 --> 00:03:06,980
The active profile is Asha, a fictional label attached to a deterministic synthetic dataset.

27
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:11,280
The profile bar states the observation count and date range.

28
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:20,309
Across the top, three cards separate current modeled systolic pressure, the chosen scenario at the selected horizon, and held-out prediction error.

29
00:03:20,309 --> 00:03:29,768
The current number is a model estimate at the most recent seven-day average habits; it is not simply the last cuff reading.

30
00:03:29,768 --> 00:03:34,067
The scenario number depends on the controls at the right.

31
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:37,507
Prediction error comes from a separate chronological evaluation.

32
00:03:37,507 --> 00:03:46,106
Keeping these three concepts distinct prevents a future scenario from being mistaken for a measured reading or an accuracy guarantee.

33
00:03:46,106 --> 00:03:50,835
Notice also the persistent research notice and the synthetic data badge.

34
00:03:50,835 --> 00:03:54,275
These disclosures remain part of the normal workflow.

35
00:03:56,775 --> 00:04:10,277
Each row contains an ISO date, systolic pressure in millimeters of mercury, daily steps, sleep hours, dietary sodium in milligrams, and stress on a zero to ten scale.

36
00:04:10,277 --> 00:04:15,582
The application accepts between twenty-eight and seven hundred thirty consecutive days.

37
00:04:15,582 --> 00:04:20,404
It checks both individual values and the sequence of dates.

38
00:04:20,404 --> 00:04:26,191
Duplicate dates, gaps, missing fields, non-finite numbers, and out-of-range values are rejected.

39
00:04:26,191 --> 00:04:30,531
These are software bounds, not recommendations for healthy behavior.

40
00:04:30,531 --> 00:04:39,693
We do not silently interpolate missing readings because doing so would introduce another modeling assumption that users might overlook.

41
00:04:39,693 --> 00:04:50,784
The browser sends CSV text to the API, which parses it into the same validated observation objects used by the JSON analysis endpoint.

42
00:04:50,784 --> 00:04:57,535
This shared contract keeps imported and synthetic workflows consistent and makes invalid-input behavior testable.

43
00:05:00,035 --> 00:05:03,778
The first modeling layer is Bayesian linear regression.

44
00:05:03,778 --> 00:05:08,456
Four standardized habit features and an intercept describe systolic pressure.

45
00:05:08,456 --> 00:05:11,263
Each person gets a separate fit.

46
00:05:11,263 --> 00:05:17,345
There is no pretrained neural network, external language model, or hidden population dataset.

47
00:05:17,345 --> 00:05:25,766
Gaussian priors regularize the coefficients so a small or correlated history does not lead to an unconstrained fit.

48
00:05:25,766 --> 00:05:31,380
The posterior mean and covariance are calculated directly using NumPy matrix operations.

49
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:38,398
The prior values are illustrative engineering choices, not clinical effect sizes copied from a trial.

50
00:05:38,398 --> 00:05:46,819
In particular, the model does not prove that increasing one habit will cause a particular change in pressure.

51
00:05:46,819 --> 00:05:51,030
It estimates an association conditional on the recorded inputs.

52
00:05:51,030 --> 00:05:59,451
The repository contains the exact feature scales, prior values, equations, noise assumptions, and limitations in the model card.

53
00:06:01,951 --> 00:06:08,049
A static regression alone would not capture the concept of an updating twin.

54
00:06:08,049 --> 00:06:14,617
PulseTwin adds a scalar Kalman filter over the residual pressure after the regression prediction.

55
00:06:14,617 --> 00:06:21,184
This state represents slow unobserved drift without naming it as a specific disease mechanism.

56
00:06:21,184 --> 00:06:30,098
Each daily residual adjusts the current state using a Kalman gain, while process variance expresses additional uncertainty over time.

57
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:38,542
When a new history is imported, the personal coefficients are refitted and the residual sequence is filtered again.

58
00:06:38,542 --> 00:06:44,171
This is a two-stage approximation, not a joint physiological state-space inference system.

59
00:06:44,171 --> 00:06:49,331
The covariance does not capture every dependency between coefficients and state.

60
00:06:49,331 --> 00:06:53,084
The implementation is a human-in-the-loop, data-driven twin prototype.

61
00:06:53,084 --> 00:07:01,997
It provides a repeatable observation and simulation loop, while continuous sensor synchronization and clinical feedback are explicitly future work.

62
00:07:04,497 --> 00:07:09,590
Now we move from the observed past to a hypothetical future.

63
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:16,534
The scenario studio exposes four controls, using the same feature definitions as the personal model.

64
00:07:16,534 --> 00:07:29,033
The default example sets movement to seven thousand five hundred steps, sleep to seven and a half hours, sodium to two thousand milligrams, and stress to four.

65
00:07:29,033 --> 00:07:34,125
These defaults are demonstration settings, not a recommendation for any person.

66
00:07:34,125 --> 00:07:40,144
After selecting Simulate scenario, the server recalculates the trajectory and the contribution breakdown.

67
00:07:40,144 --> 00:07:46,162
Habit values move gradually from the recent seven-day averages toward the chosen targets.

68
00:07:46,162 --> 00:07:53,106
The seven-day adaptation time constant is an assumption, not something learned from a clinical intervention.

69
00:07:53,106 --> 00:07:56,346
The horizon selector changes the forecast length.

70
00:07:56,346 --> 00:08:03,291
This interaction makes it possible to compare hypotheses while keeping the inputs and assumptions visible.

71
00:08:05,791 --> 00:08:09,177
The chart separates three kinds of information.

72
00:08:09,177 --> 00:08:12,562
The gray-green history is measured synthetic pressure.

73
00:08:12,562 --> 00:08:15,948
The dashed comparator holds recent habits unchanged.

74
00:08:15,948 --> 00:08:20,302
The solid green line represents the selected conditional scenario.

75
00:08:20,302 --> 00:08:29,009
Around that line, the shaded band is a ninety-five percent posterior predictive interval under the model's Gaussian assumptions.

76
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:36,748
It combines coefficient uncertainty, observation noise, residual-state uncertainty, and process variance that accumulates with the horizon.

77
00:08:36,748 --> 00:08:44,488
This is a band for possible daily readings, not a confidence interval for a treatment benefit.

78
00:08:44,488 --> 00:08:52,227
It does not account for every source of measurement error, confounding, changing medication, or model misspecification.

79
00:08:52,227 --> 00:09:00,934
The default synthetic example predicts a lower mean under the chosen settings, but the broad interval remains visible.

80
00:09:00,934 --> 00:09:06,255
A single attractive point estimate should never replace that uncertainty context.

81
00:09:08,755 --> 00:09:14,840
Below the chart, the explanation panel breaks the projected difference into four contributions.

82
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:25,607
Each contribution is the fitted personal coefficient multiplied by the standardized change in that input and the adaptation fraction at the chosen horizon.

83
00:09:25,607 --> 00:09:30,288
Before display rounding, these values sum to the scenario difference.

84
00:09:30,288 --> 00:09:36,841
This is an exact explanation of this linear simulation, not a separate explanation model.

85
00:09:36,841 --> 00:09:39,650
The signs are not artificially constrained.

86
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:45,735
With a different imported dataset, a coefficient could be small, positive, or counterintuitive.

87
00:09:45,735 --> 00:09:51,821
Correlated habits can make individual coefficients unstable, and unmeasured factors can confound them.

88
00:09:51,821 --> 00:09:57,438
The panel therefore labels them as modeled associations rather than proven effects.

89
00:09:57,438 --> 00:10:05,396
Reviewers can inspect the coefficients in the JSON export and reproduce the arithmetic directly from the source.

90
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:09,609
Transparency is useful precisely because it exposes these limitations.

91
00:10:12,109 --> 00:10:14,793
A convincing interface is not enough.

92
00:10:14,793 --> 00:10:20,607
PulseTwin evaluates the model using a chronological holdout rather than a random split.

93
00:10:20,607 --> 00:10:27,316
For the ninety-day fixtures, the first seventy-six days train the personal model and residual state.

94
00:10:27,316 --> 00:10:30,894
The final fourteen days provide the evaluation labels.

95
00:10:30,894 --> 00:10:36,261
Those held-out pressure values never enter the fit or the state update.

96
00:10:36,261 --> 00:10:47,443
The model does use the observed lifestyle covariates for those days, so this is conditional prediction rather than an honest forecast of unknown future behavior.

97
00:10:47,443 --> 00:10:55,941
We compare mean absolute error against two simple alternatives: repeating the final training pressure and repeating the training mean.

98
00:10:55,941 --> 00:10:59,072
The application also reports predictive interval coverage.

99
00:10:59,072 --> 00:11:08,464
A dedicated test changes held-out labels and confirms the predictions remain identical, directly checking for target leakage in this evaluation path.

100
00:11:10,964 --> 00:11:25,372
On the included synthetic fixtures, Asha has a twin mean absolute error of three point zero one millimeters of mercury, Dev has three point one nine, and Mira has two point eight one.

101
00:11:25,372 --> 00:11:34,104
The training-mean baselines have errors of three point six zero, three point eight five, and four point four seven respectively.

102
00:11:34,104 --> 00:11:37,597
The last-reading baselines are weaker on these fixtures.

103
00:11:37,597 --> 00:11:42,836
All fourteen held-out readings fall within the predictive interval for each profile.

104
00:11:42,836 --> 00:11:51,132
That does not establish reliable calibration, because fourteen examples are a tiny sample and the bands may be conservative.

105
00:11:51,132 --> 00:11:57,244
More importantly, the synthetic generator uses approximately linear relationships similar to the fitted model.

106
00:11:57,244 --> 00:12:02,047
These results demonstrate that the implementation behaves sensibly on its fixtures.

107
00:12:02,047 --> 00:12:08,159
They are not evidence of clinical accuracy, causal benefit, or generalization to real patients.

108
00:12:10,659 --> 00:12:15,423
The import workflow makes this more than a canned dashboard.

109
00:12:15,423 --> 00:12:21,616
In the demonstration, a supplied CSV is imported through the normal file control.

110
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:28,285
The server checks the header, values, date sequence, and minimum history before accepting it.

111
00:12:28,285 --> 00:12:36,860
The interface changes its provenance badge to imported data, and the personal model is recalculated from those observations.

112
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:46,388
Users can switch between the imported series and the synthetic profiles without losing the imported history during the current session.

113
00:12:46,388 --> 00:12:55,439
Export report downloads a JSON document containing the inputs, scenario settings, forecast, contributions, model version, warnings, and validation results.

114
00:12:55,439 --> 00:12:59,250
The separate CSV action downloads the current observations.

115
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:10,206
These files can contain sensitive records if real data is imported, so the prototype is intended for synthetic or properly authorized, de-identified use.

116
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:12,588
No cloud storage is involved.

117
00:13:15,088 --> 00:13:18,850
The implementation has a deliberately small architecture.

118
00:13:18,850 --> 00:13:23,150
A static browser application handles interaction and visualization.

119
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:30,674
FastAPI serves the interface and exposes health, synthetic profile, CSV import, and analysis endpoints.

120
00:13:30,674 --> 00:13:34,437
Pydantic validates JSON and parsed CSV observations.

121
00:13:34,437 --> 00:13:40,349
NumPy computes the Bayesian fit, filtered state, scenario, and chronological evaluation.

122
00:13:40,349 --> 00:13:47,336
The server returns a structured report, which the browser renders and can download.

123
00:13:47,336 --> 00:13:54,323
There is no database, analytics service, external model provider, or paid API dependency.

124
00:13:54,323 --> 00:13:59,697
After package installation, the application works without external network calls.

125
00:13:59,697 --> 00:14:06,147
The architecture document shows both the request flow and the trust boundary.

126
00:14:06,147 --> 00:14:14,746
This simplicity makes the prototype easy to inspect and run, but it is not production security.

127
00:14:14,746 --> 00:14:23,345
Authentication, secure deployment, retention controls, and clinical governance would be required before handling real patient workflows.

128
00:14:25,845 --> 00:14:30,452
The repository includes fourteen automated model and API tests.

129
00:14:30,452 --> 00:14:45,296
They check finite forecasts, correctly ordered intervals, a zero change when habits remain fixed, state updates with additional observations, and increasing uncertainty over the horizon when inputs are fixed.

130
00:14:45,296 --> 00:14:53,998
Other tests reject duplicate dates, missing dates, non-finite values, out-of-range readings, insufficient history, and malformed CSV data.

131
00:14:53,998 --> 00:14:58,605
The API itself is exercised through a test client.

132
00:14:58,605 --> 00:15:12,937
Browser acceptance checks use real Chromium to load the dashboard, change a scenario and horizon, switch profiles, import and reselect data, download a report, and inspect invalid-input feedback.

133
00:15:12,937 --> 00:15:19,591
A mobile-width check looks for horizontal overflow, and uncaught JavaScript errors cause failure.

134
00:15:19,591 --> 00:15:23,174
These checks demonstrate a functional prototype workflow.

135
00:15:23,174 --> 00:15:30,340
They do not substitute for security review, load testing, usability research, or medical validation.

136
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:38,077
PulseTwin includes three deterministic synthetic profiles and no patient records.

137
00:15:38,077 --> 00:15:44,362
The application has no server-side persistence and makes no external AI calls.

138
00:15:44,362 --> 00:15:53,265
Uploaded observations travel to the local API and remain in request memory and the active browser session.

139
00:15:53,265 --> 00:16:00,597
A downloaded report contains its underlying observations, so exporting is a deliberate data-handling action.

140
00:16:00,597 --> 00:16:11,071
The prototype does not have user authentication, clinical access controls, or production hardening, and it should remain local during evaluation.

141
00:16:11,071 --> 00:16:17,879
Model warnings explain observational uncertainty and identify scenarios beyond the observed input range.

142
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:24,687
Important variables such as medications, comorbidities, measurement timing, and kidney function are absent.

143
00:16:24,687 --> 00:16:28,877
Those gaps are substantive limitations, not minor disclaimers.

144
00:16:28,877 --> 00:16:37,780
The prototype helps inspect a hypothesis; it does not diagnose, prescribe, triage symptoms, or claim regulatory approval.

145
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:45,221
The next step is not simply adding more visual features.

146
00:16:45,221 --> 00:16:52,633
A credible development path starts with consented, well-characterized longitudinal data and a preregistered evaluation plan.

147
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:58,562
We would examine measurement quality, missingness, calibration, and performance across relevant subgroups.

148
00:16:58,562 --> 00:17:05,974
We would compare against stronger temporal baselines and test whether the residual state adds value.

149
00:17:05,974 --> 00:17:11,409
Clinician review would help define appropriate uses and identify failure cases.

150
00:17:11,409 --> 00:17:19,809
Any investigation of intervention effects would need a causal design rather than assuming regression coefficients are causal.

151
00:17:19,809 --> 00:17:26,233
Secure ingestion, authentication, data governance, and deletion controls must precede real patient deployment.

152
00:17:26,233 --> 00:17:31,668
Live device synchronization could then make the update loop more automatic.

153
00:17:31,668 --> 00:17:34,633
Each of these is future work.

154
00:17:34,633 --> 00:17:43,032
The present submission delivers a transparent, reproducible starting point whose assumptions and limits can be challenged directly.

155
00:17:45,532 --> 00:17:56,849
To reproduce the prototype, create a Python environment, install the pinned dependencies, and start the FastAPI application using the command in the README.

156
00:17:56,849 --> 00:18:02,753
The browser dashboard and API documentation are served from the same process.

157
00:18:02,753 --> 00:18:15,054
Run the unit tests and evaluation script to regenerate the reported metrics, and use the browser acceptance script with Chromium to check the interactive workflow.

158
00:18:15,054 --> 00:18:24,402
The repository includes the architecture PDF, project presentation, synthetic fixtures, model card, MIT license, captions, and this narration script.

159
00:18:24,402 --> 00:18:31,782
The challenge screenshot also requires accurate team and institutional information and an unlisted YouTube link.

160
00:18:31,782 --> 00:18:43,591
Those factual and account-dependent items must be completed honestly; this package does not invent them or claim that the contest form has been submitted.

161
00:18:43,591 --> 00:18:50,479
PulseTwin's contribution is a working, inspectable research prototype with reproducible evidence and explicit boundaries.
